      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is truly what you want, tell me that explicitly, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional."
      }
