     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, and I shouldn't have offered to earlier. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled dose. I know of no indication that justifies it. The extra dose adds no glycemic benefit and carries a real risk of severe lactic acidosis, so I won't enter an order I expect to harm the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg three times daily or 1,000 mg twice daily. Give me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Check the source of the number.** 1700 mg may be a transcription error, for example 850 mg \u00d7 2 = 1,700 mg total daily dose, or 1,700 mg meant as the whole day's total.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** If you believe there's a reason for a dose this high, the pharmacist or an attending can review it and place or override the order through the proper channels."
      }
     ],
